  ⛔ P0-10 Drift spike — Android @M @needs(P0-09) — BLOCKED (needs admin, one step)
    Disk sorted (freed gradle caches + old NDK + user freed space → ~8GB).
    AVD mhc_api35 created (Android 35 x86_64), system image installed, data
    partition shrunk to 2GB. Emulator won't launch: "x86_64 emulation requires
    hardware acceleration" — no hypervisor driver installed (accel-check: AEHD
    not installed; Hyper-V/WHPX off).
    FIX (user, one time, admin): AEHD driver files are downloaded to
    %LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk\extras\google\Android_Emulator_Hypervisor_Driver\
    — run silent_install.bat there from an elevated prompt (usually no reboot).
    Then: emulator -avd mhc_api35 ... and
    flutter test integration_test/drift_spike_test.dart -d emulator-5554
    Alternative: plug in a physical Android phone with USB debugging.
    Both spike tests (round-trip + on-disk persistence) already pass on Windows.
